<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Red Turban Rebellion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1351–<a href="/years/1368">1368</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Red Turban Rebellion was a series of uprisings against Mongol rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, beginning in 1351 under the influence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-lotus">White Lotus</a> millenarian beliefs and lasting to 1368. It spread across central China and produced competing warlords. One of them, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Zhu Yuanzhang</a>, defeated his rivals, drove out the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a> in 1368.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/red-turban-rebellion.jpg" alt="Red Turban Rebellion" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_Turban.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
